  "term": "folklore",
  "definition": "Folklore is shared vernacular knowledge and expression in everyday culture, such as proverbs that carry social meanings across a community. In this packet, it is presented as a form of environmental and moral reasoning that preserves and communicates norms through ordinary images, objects, and sayings.",
