      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s first sentence gives a broad, general characterization of folklore as “shared vernacular knowledge and expression in everyday culture.” The packet instead discusses “women-focused Saudi proverbs” as “eco-folklore” in a specific ecocritical framing, and does not supply a general definitional statement of folklore in these terms.",
        "The definition’s phrase “it is presented as a form of environmental and moral reasoning” is broadly consistent with the packet’s claim about “vernacular environmental reasoning embedded in gender ideology” and proverbs’ moral/disciplinary functions, but because the first sentence’s general folklore definition is not supported, the overall definition cannot be accepted as supported by the packet."
